# Build context is the repository root for all three Dockerfiles.
#
# **/node_modules is load-bearing: docker/angular.Dockerfile does
# `COPY package*.json` -> `npm ci` -> `COPY spring-petclinic-angular/ ./`.
# A host-side node_modules in the context would clobber the freshly installed
# tree in that second COPY.
#
# DO NOT add a `**/*.jar` pattern: it would strip
# spring-petclinic-rest/.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar and break the REST build
# with a very confusing error.

.git
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/target
**/dist
**/.angular
**/out-tsc
**/coverage
spring-petclinic-angular/docs
tests/test-results
tests/playwright-report
tests/blob-report
**/*.log

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
